{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"1d8b3e751b59067e","name":"card_event_chain_home","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_chain_home","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CHAIN HOME","text":"Change the attack of a friendly unit to be equal to its defense. It fights a random enemy unit.","flavorText":"Chain Home was the code name for the British early warning radar system developed before and during WWII. It was the first operational radar network in the world and became a key component of the United Kingdom’s air defense system. Construction began in the 1930s, and by the outbreak of war in 1939, a chain of radar stations had been established along the British coastline. These stations used high-frequency radio waves to detect incoming enemy aircraft at long range. Information from the radar was sent to filter rooms and command centers, where it was used to direct RAF fighter aircraft to intercept enemy bombers. Chain Home played a vital role in the defense of Britain against aerial attacks and was especially important during the Battle of Britain in 1940, as it allowed the RAF to effectively manage its limited fighter resources. The system remained operational throughout the war and was continually expanded and upgraded.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_chain_home","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_chain_home_title","SourceString":"CHAIN HOME","LocalizedString":"CHAIN HOME"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_chain_home_text","SourceString":"Change the attack of a friendly unit to be equal to its defense. It fights a random enemy unit.","LocalizedString":"Change the attack of a friendly unit to be equal to its defense. It fights a random enemy unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespa